5 Chemical aspects of fracture and sub-critical crack growth
While the possibility of chemically activated fracture at subcritical loads has been known for some decades (Lawn 1993; Michalske and Freiman 1982), accurate modelling of crack tip chemistry has only very recently become feasible as a result of advances in both modelling approaches and available supercomputing resources. The effect of environmental species on bond breaking mechanisms is a fundamental issue that is not yet fully understood. It forms part of the more general topic of stress corrosion cracking, a term also used to describe a broad class of complex and interrelated
